        "note": "Guadeloupe and La Réunion are retained as overseas regional-level surfaces while preserving their département-et-région d’outre-mer semantics rather than flattening them into ordinary metropolitan regions."
      },
      {
        "type": "martinique-guyane-single-territorial-collectivities",
        "canonicalRegionCodes": [
          "02",
          "03"
        ],
        "note": "Martinique and Guyane remain COG regional-level surfaces while their current single territorial collectivities exercise competences formerly split between department and region."
